<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Deliberately declares NO <subtype>.

    Ctrl+Space is handled by HardwareKeyboardShortcutController, which builds a
    rotation list of physical-keyboard positions. For an input method with no
    enabled subtypes it adds InputMethodSubtypeHandle.of(imi, null). The current
    position comes from IMMS.getCurrentInputMethodSubtypeLocked(), which returns
    null only when getSubtypeCount() == 0.

    So declaring even one subtype desynchronises the two: the list holds
    (ime, null) while the current position is (ime, thatSubtype), getNeighborItem
    finds no match, returns null, and Ctrl+Space does nothing while this IME is
    selected - the user can only switch away from Gboard, never back.

    With no subtype both sides agree on (ime, null), and IMMS.
    switchKeyboardLayoutLocked has an explicit subtypeCount == 0 branch that
    selects this IME with NOT_A_SUBTYPE_ID. The physical keyboard layout is
    still assigned per input method in Settings, which is how it already
    appeared.
-->
<input-method xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:supportsSwitchingToNextInputMethod="true" />
